{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"options":{"content":"","images":{},"widgets":{}},"type":"multiple"},"hints":[{"content":"We will solve this by integrating by parts. We know that \n\n$\\qquad\\displaystyle\\int u(x)v\\,^\\prime(x)dx = u(x)v(x)-\\int u\\,^\\prime(x)v(x)dx\\,$.\n\nWe can rewrite this as\n\n$\\qquad\\displaystyle\\int u\\ dv = uv-\\int v\\ du\\,$.","images":{},"widgets":{}},{"content":"In this problem we will let $~u = \\tan^{-1}x~$ and $~dv=dx\\,$.","images":{},"widgets":{}},{"content":"Then $~du = \\dfrac{1}{x^2+1}~$ and $~v = \\displaystyle\\int dx = x\\,$.","images":{},"widgets":{}},{"content":"Integration by parts gives\n\n$\\displaystyle\\qquad\\int \\tan^{-1}x\\,dx = x\\tan^{-1}x-\\int\\dfrac{x}{x^2+1}\\,dx$\n\n$\\displaystyle\\qquad\\qquad\\qquad~~~~~\\,=x\\tan^{-1}x-\\dfrac12\\ln(x^2+1)+C\\,$.","images":{},"widgets":{}}],"question":{"content":"Evaluate $~~\\displaystyle\\int \\tan^{-1}x\\,dx\\,$.\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$\\tan^{-1}x-\\ln(x^2+1)+C$","correct":false},{"content":"$x\\tan^{-1}x-\\ln x+C$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\tan^{-1}x-\\dfrac12\\ln(x^2+1)+C$","correct":false},{"content":"$x\\tan^{-1}x-\\dfrac12\\ln(x^2+1)+C$","correct":true}],"displayCount":null,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":true,"randomize":false},"type":"radio","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}}}
